  <wpt lat="49.6242824285215" lon="-123.9841588656956">
    <name>Route Alternative</name>
    <cmt>control</cmt>
    <desc>Riders could choose to take main road here instead of trails</desc>
    <sym>Dot</sym>
    <type>checkpoint</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="49.37408916982879" lon="-123.27238999697195">
    <name>Squamish Bike</name>
    <cmt>transit</cmt>
    <desc>If you want to avoid the ride to Squamish on the main road you can use this bus service. Bikes are free.</desc>
    <sym>Dot</sym>
    <type>transport</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="49.38984287798087" lon="-123.25574243411401">
    <name>Sea to Sky Highway</name>
    <cmt>caution</cmt>
    <desc>A fairly busy highway to Squamish. But most of the route has an OK shoulder and the scenery is nice. But still need to ride cautiously on some stretches. Take the shuttle if you don't like hwy riding.</desc>
    <sym>Dot</sym>
    <type>danger</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="48.914733186821174" lon="-124.47710486260506">
    <name>Logging activity possible for next several miles</name>
    <cmt>caution</cmt>
    <sym>Dot</sym>
    <type>danger</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="50.31328477423477" lon="-122.7914521873126">
    <name>Limited services for next 140km to Liloet</name>
    <cmt>caution</cmt>
    <desc>Also expect some areas with no cell service</desc>
    <sym>Dot</sym>
    <type>danger</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="49.26745091088372" lon="-124.74154927137411">
    <name>Big Climb</name>
    <cmt>caution</cmt>
    <desc>Includes a steep rocky uphill section that may require some hike-a-bike push</desc>
    <sym>Dot</sym>
    <type>danger</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="49.45024599450238" lon="-124.738494002355">
    <name>HWY 19A</name>
    <cmt>caution</cmt>
    <desc>Fairly high traffic, but good shoulder</desc>
    <sym>Dot</sym>
    <type>danger</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="49.87450626701126" lon="-124.4861018406672">
    <name>Route Alternative</name>
    <cmt>control</cmt>
    <desc>Riders can choose to take this road south instead of this trail option.</desc>
    <sym>Dot</sym>
    <type>checkpoint</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="49.59606603310036" lon="-123.99547750098108">
    <name>Copperhead Trail</name>
    <cmt>trailhead</cmt>
    <sym>Dot</sym>
    <type>info</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="50.70189565031953" lon="-121.9140124592338">
    <name>Main Road Riding</name>
    <cmt>caution</cmt>
    <desc>Moderately busy paved road to Ashcroft. Likely busier during peak tourist season.  But reasonable shoulder most of the way.</desc>
    <sym>Dot</sym>
    <type>danger</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="49.691363482377625" lon="-123.96234314159652">
    <name>Route Alternative</name>
    <cmt>control</cmt>
    <desc>Riders can choose to stay on main road here instead of trail option</desc>
    <sym>Dot</sym>
    <type>checkpoint</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="49.500417265113455" lon="-123.82873863655297">
    <name>A little bit of hike-a-bike here</name>
    <cmt>caution</cmt>
    <sym>Dot</sym>
    <type>danger</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="49.497288928649866" lon="-123.80944571431576">
    <name>Some rocky stuff here</name>
    <cmt>caution</cmt>
    <sym>Dot</sym>
    <type>danger</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="49.46676373008804" lon="-123.7422738008421">
    <name>Need to carry bike down rocky barrier</name>
    <cmt>caution</cmt>
    <sym>Dot</sym>
    <type>danger</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="49.464309776382855" lon="-123.74070507045087">
    <name>Busy road</name>
    <cmt>caution</cmt>
    <desc>Somewhat adequate shoulder</desc>
    <sym>Dot</sym>
    <type>danger</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="49.885029243214" lon="-123.17992647675042">
    <name>Flooded Trail?</name>
    <cmt>caution</cmt>
    <desc>There is a short section of trail here that is prone to flooding. But the trail starts again shortly after the flooded section and it should not be too deep of a crossing.</desc>
    <sym>Dot</sym>
    <type>danger</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="49.89130317935269" lon="-123.18104104046868">
    <name>Rocky trail</name>
    <cmt>caution</cmt>
    <desc>Start of some rough trail hike-a-bike</desc>
    <sym>Dot</sym>
    <type>danger</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="49.89895591763126" lon="-123.1761438202047">
    <name>Some annoying barriers that require lifting bike over.</name>
    <cmt>caution</cmt>
    <sym>Dot</sym>
    <type>danger</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="49.90571242111113" lon="-123.17454290615643">
    <name>More rocky hike-a-bike</name>
    <cmt>caution</cmt>
    <sym>Dot</sym>
    <type>danger</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="50.314611388545856" lon="-122.79877493392944">
    <name>Turn here to go into town</name>
    <cmt>generic</cmt>
    <sym>Dot</sym>
    <type>generic</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="50.552955071337365" lon="-122.48386861616308">
    <name>Hard Road</name>
    <cmt>caution</cmt>
    <desc>The road to Seton Portage can be rough and very steep in spots. It's a tough ride with some life-questioning moments. But hopefully the fantastic scenery will be worth it for you.</desc>
    <sym>Dot</sym>
    <type>danger</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="50.70873509107428" lon="-122.28229792098365">
    <name>No services until Lillooet</name>
    <cmt>caution</cmt>
    <sym>Dot</sym>
    <type>danger</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="50.704530124909496" lon="-121.28090363756124">
    <name>Start of 16km of climbing. Not too steep</name>
    <cmt>caution</cmt>
    <sym>Dot</sym>
    <type>danger</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="50.716266151979795" lon="-121.28083721155916">
    <name>Services</name>
    <cmt>caution</cmt>
    <desc>No services until Logan Lake. About 80km</desc>
    <sym>Dot</sym>
    <type>danger</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="50.71626580847025" lon="-120.8433840017739">
    <name>Steep climb with no water</name>
    <cmt>caution</cmt>
    <sym>Dot</sym>
    <type>danger</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="49.42082000000002" lon="-123.63831">
    <name>Route Alternative</name>
    <cmt>control</cmt>
    <desc>Riders who want to avoid the trail option to the Langdale ferry can take this paved route. </desc>
    <sym>Dot</sym>
    <type>checkpoint</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="50.08165989855475" lon="-123.03734722516043">
    <name>Cheakamus Lake Extension</name>
    <cmt>control</cmt>
    <desc>A very worthy detour ride to Cheakamus Lake within  Garibaldi Provincial Park . A mixture of gravel road and singletrack. Amazing views and old growth forest. A couple of camping options. Reservations should be made in advance here: https://bcparks.ca/reservations/backcountry-camping/garibaldi/</desc>
    <sym>Dot</sym>
    <type>checkpoint</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="50.08155317521849" lon="-123.05128244070073">
    <name>Route option</name>
    <cmt>control</cmt>
    <desc>Optional out-and-back to suspension bridge and train wreck site.</desc>
    <sym>Dot</sym>
    <type>checkpoint</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="49.29961435643537" lon="-124.7463889422761">
    <name>Look for trail/road to Lucy Lake here. Don't go down new logging road on left.</name>
    <cmt>generic</cmt>
    <sym>Dot</sym>
    <type>generic</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="50.27271142738445" lon="-122.8678441047312">
    <name>Route Alternative</name>
    <cmt>control</cmt>
    <desc>Riders can choose to take main road into Pemberton instead of trail.</desc>
    <sym>Dot</sym>
    <type>checkpoint</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="48.89922611683292" lon="-124.6886354147277">
    <name>Route Alternative</name>
    <cmt>control</cmt>
    <desc>It's possible to take this more exciting route to Port Alberni. Dirt forest service road to Bamfield and then a beautiful boat ride up the Alberni Inlet to Port Alberni. Make note of the days the boat runs and the need to reserve a spot.</desc>
    <sym>Dot</sym>
    <type>checkpoint</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="49.64442344090409" lon="-124.94748228203235">
    <name>Route Altenrative</name>
    <cmt>control</cmt>
    <desc>Riders who need a shorter route can take this trail all the way into Courtenay. </desc>
    <sym>Dot</sym>
    <type>checkpoint</type>
  </wpt>
