    <name>Route Alternative</name>
    <cmt>control</cmt>
    <desc>Riders who wish to take in a little coastal scenery can use this routing option. A longer ride on the Galloping Goose trail, followed by a ride on the main road between Sooke and Port Renfrew. Traffic is moderate on that section and there are several access points to beaches. This is followed by the excellent gravel Gordon River road to meet up with the GNBR at Halfmoon Bay. </desc>
    <sym>Dot</sym>
    <type>checkpoint</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="50.31818641009531" lon="-122.8019862133054">
    <name>Route Alternative</name>
    <cmt>control</cmt>
    <desc>Here is another excellent adventurous route towards Lillooet. It goes up the stunning Hurly Pass and also takes the excellent road along Carpenter Lake. Expect snow to linger longer in the season in this area. </desc>
